  "summary": "Phidias was an Athenian sculptor whose gold-and-ivory statues of Athena in the Parthenon and of Zeus at Olympia made him the most celebrated artist of classical antiquity. Pericles put him in charge of artistic projects in Athens; the Athena was dedicated in 438 BCE and the Zeus finished in 430 BCE.",
